<title>MEXICO: Ahmsa negotiates export-backed credit.</title>
<headline>Ahmsa negotiates export-backed credit.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican steel producer Altos Hornos de Mexico (Ahmsa) has negotiated a two-tranche $330 million export backed credit, a company official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have practically concluded it; it will be three or four days before everything is ready,&quot; said the company official, who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>The credit was arranged by J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p>The company official said that $140 million will be used to refinance already existing export backed debt instruments, thus reducing the average cost and lengthening the maturity.</p>
<p>The other $190 million will be used mainly to refinance dollar-denominated debt, the official said.</p>
<p>The official said overall company debt will not increase with the credit.</p>
<p>((-- Monterrey newsroom (525) +528 3457617))</p>
